Frappe Version: 16.18.3
### Description

When a file is uploaded or cleared via an `Attach` field (`ControlAttach`), the control calls `this.frm.save()` unconditionally. This triggers the full save pipeline — including mandatory field validation — even when the rest of the form is incomplete or in a draft/new state. This occurs even uploading attachment in childt table. 

The result is a **"Missing Fields"** dialog that blocks the user, despite the user only intending to attach a file, not submit the document.

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Open a new document that has mandatory fields (e.g. Sales Order — Customer, Item Code, Delivery Date, UOM are all required).
2. Without filling in the mandatory fields, upload a file via an `Attach`-type field.
3. Observe the **Missing Fields** dialog appearing immediately after upload completes.

Same behavior occurs when clicking **Clear** on an already-attached file.

### Expected Behavior

Uploading or clearing an attachment should only update the attachment field and its related UI state. It should not force the form into a dirty/savable state or trigger the full save flow outside of the normal model update pipeline.

### Actual Behavior

`on_upload_complete` and `clear_attachment` both call `this.frm.save()` unconditionally:

```js
// on_upload_complete
async on_upload_complete(attachment) {
    if (this.frm) {
        await this.parse_validate_and_set_in_model(attachment.file_url);
        this.frm.attachments.update_attachment(attachment);
        this.frm.doc.docstatus == 1 ? this.frm.save("Update") : this.frm.save(); // ← triggers full save
    }
    this.set_value(attachment.file_url);
}

// clear_attachment
me.frm.attachments.remove_attachment_by_filename(me.value, async () => {
    await me.parse_validate_and_set_in_model(null);
    me.refresh();
    me.frm.doc.docstatus == 1 ? me.frm.save("Update") : me.frm.save(); // ← triggers full save
});
```

### Suggested Fix

Guard the `frm.save()` call so it only runs when the document has already been saved at least once (i.e. `!this.frm.is_new()`), or defer to the user to explicitly save after attaching:

```js
async on_upload_complete(attachment) {
    if (this.frm) {
        await this.parse_validate_and_set_in_model(attachment.file_url);
        this.frm.attachments.update_attachment(attachment);
        if (!this.frm.is_new()) {
            this.frm.doc.docstatus == 1 ? this.frm.save("Update") : this.frm.save();
        }
    }
    this.set_value(attachment.file_url);
}
```

Apply the same guard in `clear_attachment`.

### Impact

This affects any DocType that has both an `Attach` field and other mandatory fields — the attachment interaction unintentionally breaks the new-document workflow by surfacing validation errors prematurely.

### Screenshots

<img width="1580" height="900" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2cc7a46e-4cb8-4607-a44b-019c063a3269" />

@GursheenK @iamejaaz

